  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The floral wallpaper cover of this artist's book invokes the Domestic Site of its title, leaving the rest of the book to address the subtitle: Contested Terrain. Empassioned, politically engaged letters from the author to local and national politicians, public figures and political organizations are interwoven with letters to friends, journal entries and other less official though no less urgent writing about women's social, cultural and political inequality. Sexual harassment in the workplace, women's reproductive rights, HIV/AIDS, and women's unequal earning power share the stage with more academic debates about female subjectivity in this one-woman wake up call to the feminist consciousness of her readers." --Printed Matter website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
